-- הסכם קיבוצי (31.8.2016) — החלת עלות הסכם המסגרת ופרקי זמן השהייה לקידום
-- בדרגות: an interim agreement, in force until the collective agreement
-- that is to anchor the parties' wider understandings is signed. It puts
-- off the first allocation of the 2016 agreement (22.2.2016) — 1% of the
-- salary base, in uniform shekels — from 1.9.2016 to 1.10.2016; and from
-- 1.9.2016 it rewrites §38(ב) and (ו) of the base agreement, as the supreme
-- follow-up committee's decision of 19.2.2015 had worded them, in months:
-- 26, 26, 37, 37, 37 to grades 2–6 and 38 to each of grades 7–9.
--
-- It amends §38 as the decision of 19.2.2015 left it, so it imports that
-- decision's module and the base agreement's §38, and writes only the
-- months it changes, dated. The 2016 agreement, the 2013 agreement, the
-- general framework agreement and its amendment are not encoded: what this
-- agreement takes from them is an input, named.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `2015-02-19_ofek-hadash_vaadat-maakav_darga-stay-periods-1800-quota`

§ `הסכם קיבוצי — החלת עלות הסכם המסגרת ופרקי זמן השהייה — 31.8.2016`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The document's title; no rule.

-- The day of signing, written in by hand.
@ref akn:preamble/p2
`the signing of the 31.8.2016 agreement` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2016

-- akn:preamble/p3 The registration stamp under the Collective Agreements Law (15.01.2017, no. 269/2016); no rule.

-- The parties: the State, by the Treasury's (acting) wages commissioner and
-- the Ministry of Education's director-general, and the teachers' union, by
-- its secretary-general.
@ref akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8
`the 31.8.2016 agreement's parties` MEANS LIST `the State`, `the teachers' union`

-- akn:preamble/p6 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p9 "On the other side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p10 A recital: the 2013 agreement (17.9.2013) bound the parties to negotiate applying a framework agreement's cost for 27.8.2013–30.6.2015; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p11 A recital: the general framework agreement of 18.4.2016 for 1.1.2013–31.12.2017; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p12 A recital: the 2016 agreement of 22.2.2016 applied that cost to teaching employees; §§2–3 below take it as an input.
-- akn:preamble/p13 A recital: under §15 of the 2013 agreement and the framework's amendment of 8.8.2016, the parties negotiated a wage agreement to 30.6.2018; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p14 A recital: the 2016 agreement's cost is to be allotted otherwise, with further changes; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p15 A recital: no agreed wording of the agreement that will anchor it yet; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p16 A recital: some of the 2016 agreement's provisions start on 1.9.2016; §3 puts one off.

-- The understandings here apply for the time being, until a collective
-- agreement anchoring the wider understandings is signed; its provisions
-- then replace these.
@ref akn:preamble/p17
GIVEN `the replacing agreement was signed on` IS A MAYBE DATE, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 31.8.2016 agreement is in force on` `the replacing agreement was signed on` d IF
        d `is on or after` `the signing of the 31.8.2016 agreement`
    AND (CONSIDER `the replacing agreement was signed on`
         WHEN JUST s THEN NOT d `is on or after` s
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)

#ASSERT `the 31.8.2016 agreement is in force on` NOTHING (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `the 31.8.2016 agreement is in force on` (JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2016)) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2016)

-- akn:preamble/p18 A recital: the parties anchor what they agreed in this agreement; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p19 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

§§ `1 הוראות כלליות`

DECLARE `part of the 31.8.2016 agreement` IS ONE OF `its recitals`, `its clauses`

-- (א): the preamble is an inseparable part of the agreement.
@ref akn:art_1__para_a
GIVEN p IS A `part of the 31.8.2016 agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `binds as the 31.8.2016 agreement` p IF
    TRUE

#ASSERT `binds as the 31.8.2016 agreement` `its recitals`

DECLARE `word form in the 31.8.2016 agreement` IS ONE OF `the masculine form`, `the feminine form`, `the singular form`, `the plural form`

-- (ב)–(ג): masculine reads feminine and the reverse, singular plural and
-- the reverse, unless expressly stated otherwise.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b akn:art_1__para_c
GIVEN `written in` IS A `word form in the 31.8.2016 agreement`, `read in` IS A `word form in the 31.8.2016 agreement`, `expressly limited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a word of the 31.8.2016 agreement reads in another form` `written in` `read in` `expressly limited` IF
    (NOT `expressly limited`) OR `written in` EQUALS `read in`

#ASSERT `a word of the 31.8.2016 agreement reads in another form` `the masculine form` `the feminine form` FALSE

-- (ד): the headings are for convenience and nothing is learnt from them.
@ref akn:art_1__para_d
GIVEN `the reading without the headings` IS A STRING, `the reading the headings suggest` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the reading the 31.8.2016 agreement takes` `the reading without the headings` `the reading the headings suggest` IS
    `the reading without the headings`

§§ `2 תחולה`

-- Every employee on the teaching employees' scale whom the 2016 agreement
-- covers ("עובדי הוראה"). The 2016 agreement is not encoded: whether it
-- covers him is an input.
@ref akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN `on the teaching employees' scale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `covered by the 2016 agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the collective agreement of 22.2.2016, which is not encoded
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `covered by the 31.8.2016 agreement` `on the teaching employees' scale` `covered by the 2016 agreement` IF
    `on the teaching employees' scale` AND `covered by the 2016 agreement`

§§ `3 תיקון הסכם 2016`

-- The allocation §5(א)(1) of the 2016 agreement made from 1.9.2016, in
-- uniform shekels, is put off to 1.10.2016: "from 1.10.2016 — 1% on the
-- basis of the salary set out in section 6 below", allotted in uniform
-- shekels to the employees this agreement covers. The words replace those
-- of §5(א)(1), so "section 6 below" is §6 of the 2016 agreement (the
-- average monthly salary of 2015), an input here.
@ref akn:art_3/p1
`the first allocation was due under the 2016 agreement on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016
`the first allocation is made from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2016
`the first allocation's rate` MEANS 1%

GIVEN `the salary base of §6 of the 2016 agreement` IS A NUMBER @desc the monthly average for January–December 2015 of the components §6(א) of the 2016 agreement lists, for all the employees covered
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the cost of the first allocation on` `the salary base of §6 of the 2016 agreement` d IS
    IF d `is on or after` `the first allocation is made from`
    THEN `the first allocation's rate` TIMES `the salary base of §6 of the 2016 agreement`
    ELSE 0

-- "In uniform shekels": the same sum to every teacher with the same share of
-- a position, whatever his grade or pay (the 2016 agreement's §5(א)'s own
-- definition), so a teacher's part is the sum for a full position times his
-- share. The sum per full position is the 2016 agreement's, an input.
GIVEN `the sum for a full position` IS A NUMBER, `position share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a teacher's part of a uniform-shekel allocation` `the sum for a full position` `position share` IS
    `the sum for a full position` `pro rata to a position of` `position share`

#ASSERT `the cost of the first allocation on` 1000000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2016) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the cost of the first allocation on` 1000000 `the first allocation is made from` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `a teacher's part of a uniform-shekel allocation` 200 0.5 EQUALS 100

§§ `4 קידום בדרגות — תיקון סעיף 38 כנוסחו בהחלטת ועדת המעקב מיום 19.2.2015`

-- (א): for the teaching employees to whom §38 of the base agreement, as
-- amended from time to time, applies.
@ref akn:art_4__para_a
GIVEN `§38 applies to him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§4 of the 31.8.2016 agreement reaches` `§38 applies to him` IF
    `§38 applies to him`

`1 September 2016` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016

-- akn:art_4__para_b The opening of (ב): from 1.9.2016, (1) and (2).

-- (ב)(1): §38(ב), as the decision of 19.2.2015 worded it, reads: from grade
-- 1 to 2 and 2 to 3, 26 months in the grade below; from 3 to 4, 4 to 5 and
-- 5 to 6, 37 months.
@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_1
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months in the grade below for promotion to grades 2–6 from 1.9.2016` `to grade` IS
    BRANCH IF `to grade` AT MOST 3 THEN 26
           OTHERWISE 37

-- (ב)(2): §38(ו) reads: from 6 to 7, 7 to 8 and 8 to 9, 38 months.
@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months in the grade below for promotion to grades 7–9 from 1.9.2016` `to grade` IS
    38

-- (ג): (ב)(1)–(2) apply also to teachers who would have been entitled to a
-- promotion from 1.9.2016 on but for this agreement: the day that decides is
-- the day the promotion would have fallen due under the periods before
-- (convention dates.start: 1.9.2016 itself is in). Before it, the decision
-- of 19.2.2015 governs, and before 1.3.2015 the base agreement.
@ref akn:art_4__para_c
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER, `would have been due on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months in the grade below asked from 1.9.2016` `to grade` `would have been due on` IS
    IF `would have been due on` `is on or after` `1 September 2016`
    THEN IF `to grade` AT MOST 6
         THEN `months in the grade below for promotion to grades 2–6 from 1.9.2016` `to grade`
         ELSE `months in the grade below for promotion to grades 7–9 from 1.9.2016` `to grade`
    ELSE `months in the grade below for promotion to` `to grade` `would have been due on`

#ASSERT map (GIVEN g YIELD `months in the grade below asked from 1.9.2016` g `1 September 2016`) (range 2 9) EQUALS LIST 26, 26, 37, 37, 37, 38, 38, 38
#ASSERT map (GIVEN g YIELD `months in the grade below asked from 1.9.2016` g (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2016)) (range 2 9) EQUALS LIST 25, 25, 37, 37, 37, 37, 37, 37
#ASSERT `months in the grade below asked from 1.9.2016` 2 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2015) EQUALS 24
-- What changed on 1.9.2016: a month more to grades 2, 3 and 7–9, none to 4–6.
#ASSERT map (GIVEN g YIELD `months in the grade below asked from 1.9.2016` g `1 September 2016` MINUS `months in the grade below asked from 1.9.2016` g (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2016)) (range 2 9) EQUALS LIST 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1

-- (ד): nothing in §4 takes from the rest of the base agreement as amended,
-- or from other collective understandings on promotion, unless it says so:
-- §38(ט) of the decision of 19.2.2015 stands, imported.
-- F-ofek-hadash-2016-stay-periods-a: from 1.9.2016 the waiting period to
-- grade 7 is 38 months, and the longest a qualified teacher may be held
-- back from grade 7 is still three years and a month, 37. The reading
-- adopted (convention reading.every-word): the hold-back is counted from
-- the day he met the conditions of §38(ה), not from his entry to the
-- grade below — counted from the entry, the base agreement's own (ט) for
-- grade 7 (three years) would equal its waiting period and do nothing.
@ref akn:art_4__para_d
`§4 leaves §38(ט) as the decision of 19.2.2015 worded it` MEANS TRUE

`the grade-7 hold-back is shorter than the stay it follows` MEANS
    `months a qualified teacher may be held back from` 7 `1 September 2016` LESS THAN `months in the grade below asked from 1.9.2016` 7 `1 September 2016`
#ASSERT `the grade-7 hold-back is shorter than the stay it follows`

-- Counted from the entry to the grade below, the base agreement's hold-back
-- from grade 7 is its waiting period exactly.
#ASSERT `years a qualified teacher may be held back from` 7 EQUALS `years in the grade below for promotion to` 7

-- Read from the day the conditions were met: held back 37 months since
-- meeting them, with a free place, he goes first.
#ASSERT `goes before the scores under the 2015 hold-back` 7 37 1 `1 September 2016`

§§ `5 מיצוי תביעות ושקט תעשייתי`

-- Nothing here takes from, or adds to, the exhaustion of claims and the
-- industrial peace that bind the parties.
@ref akn:art_5/p1
`the 31.8.2016 agreement leaves exhaustion and industrial peace as they are` MEANS TRUE

